  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug is implicated in targeting Thioredoxin, a mitochondrial protein, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds—Phorone, Flavipin, and Interiorin—each of which ultimately binds to CD276 antigen. This indicates a conserved pathway where 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may act as a modulator of the Thioredoxin pathway, influencing CD276 antigen expression or function. The high scores across the three paths suggest a robust, biologically plausible link, though the exact mechanism of interaction between 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone and CD276 antigen remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway involving Thioredoxin and its downstream targets, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the drug’s direct effect on CD276 antigen.",
